{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"piscine-terrorful-sablefish","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nEvaluate the current rebar repository for code quality, architectural quality, documentation quality (discoverability, understandability, and context efficiency), and test quality (behavioral, contractual, and external-integration coverage; avoidance of vacuous/change-detector tests; shared fixtures; and test hygiene). This is a read-only assessment; do not modify production or test files.\n\n## Plan\n- Map the implementation and package boundaries, dependency directions, public interfaces, state ownership, and high-complexity hotspots.\n- Sample representative production paths for correctness, cohesion, readability, typing, error handling, and maintainability.\n- Trace the documentation entry points, indexes, cross-links, generated references, architecture/ADR coverage, contributor guidance, and duplicated context.\n- Inventory and sample unit, interface/contract, integration, property, golden, snapshot, subprocess, and external-service tests; inspect fixture reuse, isolation, determinism, assertions, skips, and CI execution.\n- Run read-only repository quality gates and targeted test-collection/coverage diagnostics where safe.\n- Report evidence-backed strengths and prioritized findings with exact citations, confidence, and remediation guidance.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The report assesses code quality with evidence and representative citations.\n- [ ] The report assesses architectural boundaries, dependency direction, cohesion, and extension surfaces with evidence.\n- [ ] The report assesses documentation discoverability, understandability, accuracy signals, and context efficiency with evidence.\n- [ ] The report assesses behavioral, contractual, and external-integration test coverage with evidence.\n- [ ] The report assesses vacuous/change-detector risk, fixture reuse, isolation, determinism, and test hygiene with evidence.\n- [ ] Material findings have a severity, impact explanation, and concrete remedy.\n- [ ] The final evaluation distinguishes verified observations from sampling limits and records conclusions on this ticket.","id":"ae1b-b2a0-a080-4b4e","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["audit","code-quality","architecture","documentation","testing"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Comprehensive code, architecture, documentation, and test quality evaluation"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786210343616958001,"uuid":"276bac73-c55e-4b6a-81e5-14e770557f0b"}